From 0d6087400fec6c0017af9ca0d1560ba920e87ec0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:05:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: review of the user documentation

The Sphinx documentation and the Markdown files at the root were checked
against the code (139 findings, 128 fixed here):

- the documentation describes the gpu-proto branch, not the master one;
  new section "Building the prototype" (versions of MGIS and TFEL
  required, MFEM_DIR, CMake options, HIP, Kokkos);
- batch computations: fallback of the integration by batches with
  --execution, default computation of the post-processings,
  BehaviourExecutionLocation only changes the expected location of the
  behaviour, options of mfem_mgis_add_behaviours_library, use of
  --execution and getBehavioursLibrary in the example, test cases of the
  measurements defined;
- code snippets matching the API (Context arguments, names of the
  prediction operators, MeanThermodynamicForces, quotes of the strategy of
  BoomerAMG, material argument of FBar, quadrature functions, validator
  with description, dict for FBar, may_throw instead of the deprecated
  throwing attribute), all compiled against the headers;
- simulation: roles of TimeIncrementComputer and TimeStepValidator, factor
  after a failure; benchmark page using the current profiling API;
- tutorial, glossary, commented examples, options and default values of
  the polycrystal and the cermet.

sphinx-build -W gives no warning, as before.
